    "created_at": "2021-03-21T00:07:52Z",
    "updated_at": "2021-03-21T00:07:52Z",
    "body": "I'm not sure the exact reasons why the multiple attribute was only implemented for emails, however I suspect it might be related to delimiters as you mentioned - emails don't contain commas, however ordinary text can, so a default delimiter doesn't work on arbitrary text. Working on arbitrary text without commas would seem reasonable, but it's not a perfect solution. \r\n\r\nSo yes. A delimiter attribute would be ideal - a way to specify multiple delimiters more so (although I'm not sure there would be a reasonable way to do this, so it would probably require JS)\r\n\r\n   \r\n\r\n\r\n",
